# Database Conventions

## NoSQL — MongoDB with Beanie

- Use [Beanie](https://beanie-odm.dev/) as the ODM for all MongoDB interactions
- Define documents by subclassing `beanie.Document`
- Use Beanie's built-in async methods (`find`, `find_one`, `save`, `delete`, etc.)
- Never use PyMongo directly — always go through Beanie

```python
# ✅ GOOD
class User(Document):
    name: str
    email: str

    class Settings:
        name = "users"

user = await User.find_one(User.email == "a@b.com")

# ❌ BAD — raw PyMongo
db["users"].find_one({"email": "a@b.com"})
```

## General
- Keep DB logic out of route handlers — use repository or service modules
